boopis
======

The application's own code is not released under an open licence: the repository's Cargo.toml says `UNLICENSED`.

What it carries, and under what terms:

- Hermes Agent, unmodified, inside the runtime archive /usr/lib/boopis/runtime/hermes-runtime-linux-x86_64.tar.zst.
  MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research. The licence text is hermes-agent-LICENSE, beside this file.
- The runtime also holds a Python interpreter, uv and Hermes's locked Python dependencies. Each carries its own licence
  files inside the archive; they are unpacked on first run into the application's data folder.
- The fonts the interface embeds (Fontsource packages: Geist, IBM Plex, Instrument Sans, JetBrains Mono, Libre Franklin),
  each under its own licence. The texts are in the fonts/ directory beside this file.
- WebKitGTK and GTK are not carried: the package depends on the system's.
